  "text": "The first thing to understand about the ingest pipeline is that it is asynchronous from end to end. Nothing blocks on the provider, and nothing blocks on the transcode. A recording arrives, a row is written, and a job is enqueued. That job asks object storage for a signed URL and hands it to the vendor. Minutes later the vendor says it is finished and a second job fetches the result. Only then do we write segments, and only then does the editor have anything to show. The reason this matters is that every one of those steps can fail independently. If the vendor is throttling us we back off without burning the attempt budget. If the audio is silent the vendor tells us so and we stop rather than paying twice. And if the transcode fails the transcript is still perfectly usable.",
